# Core Equity Current Automation State

This file is the short living snapshot for "where are we now?" questions. Keep the full history in `rag/memory/project_state.md`; update this file after major backend/data/RAG milestones.

## Operating Map Pointer

- Main compact product map: `rag/memory/core_equity_operating_map.md`.
- Use the operating map first for product direction, current reality, disabled surfaces, and best next action.
- Use this file for current counters, endpoint milestones, and latest operational facts.
- Use `rag/memory/project_state.md` only for detailed chronology.
- Current project meaning in one line: Core Equity is still building trustworthy data and route proof; it is not ready for client signals, trades, labels, or weak DEX mappings.

## Snapshot

- Last updated: 2026-05-19.
- Product mode: economical, admin-gated, read-only-first.
- Alpha Lab UI: frozen.
- Client trading automation: OFF.
- Wallet transactions: OFF.
- External providers and scraping: OFF by default.
- Real CEX/DEX business writes: disabled unless a separate admin-confirmed flow explicitly allows one narrow mutation.
- Hermes Agent: installed on drive D: but authorized only as a read-only analyst/reviewer until a separate integration goal changes that.
- Final product direction clarified: Core Equity is not meant to stay a manual review machine. The target is an autonomous policy engine with data collection, intelligence, risk gating, shadow trading, paper trading, and only later controlled real execution under client policy/opt-in.
- Multi-market direction clarified: Core Equity should eventually support spot, perps, memecoin manipulation detection, EVM/BSC/Ethereum/Binance context, and Solana, but these are separate lanes. Spot/EVM data quality is the near-term lane; perps need funding/open-interest/depth/liquidation data; Solana needs a dedicated parser/model instead of EVM assumptions.
- Trade Agent position-management direction clarified: future large upside such as x50/x100 is treated as a rare tail scenario, not a promise. The agent should seek asymmetry through small controlled risk, fast invalidation, partial take profits, runner logic, trailing stops, and strict kill switches, not uncontrolled leverage.

## Current Simple Position

- We are still in the data-quality foundation phase, not client automation.
- The current work is building trustworthy raw/curated DEX data before any AI trade agent can be trusted. The Trade Agent remains future-only; it may eventually propose entries/exits, but the Policy/Risk Engine must be able to block it.
- Hermes, Spark/Rawls/Bacon, and local Qwen are sidecars only. They can review, summarize, compare, and challenge decisions, but they do not operate Core Equity, write DB state, trade, create labels, or create opt-ins.
- Existing useful detection foundation: adaptive accumulation scan, strategy matrix/backtest, wallet profiles, cluster scan, manipulation casefile/readiness, CEX deposit/funding context, raw Swap provenance, and venue/source repair. The blocker is not "no logic"; it is data quality, coverage, speed, and policy-controlled evaluation.
- Current strongest usable direction is no longer "pick one token manually"; it is to grow and clean the local DEX dataset until the system can discover candidates itself. The latest source-backed curated set has 19 curated DEX facts, 12 token groups, and only 1 usable clean dataset, so it is still research-only.
- Current leading research examples are `STAR`, `IBS`, and the HAQI token row on BSC, but none is a client signal. `STAR` has the most source-backed rows but still too little wallet/pool diversity; `IBS` and HAQI are too thin. The system is not manipulation-ready yet.
- The immediate blocker is data quality and route truth: current local data has 418 swaps, 16,860 token transfers, 374 observed tokens, 95 unknown-symbol tokens, 296 Unknown DEX swaps, and 50 unknown router contracts. Core Equity must keep improving token metadata, but router/venue identity is now the bigger blocker before any label, mapping, signal, or trade.
- Latest source-quality progress: Core Equity found and persisted one source-backed DEX router evidence row for OKX DEX on BNB Chain, address `0x62ccef0b4545166f721caa9fee13c1d3767e27dc`, using official OKX smart-contract docs. A confirmed source-backed mapping then classified this router as `OKX DEX` and reclassified 9 local swaps from Unknown DEX to source-backed OKX DEX. This is data quality only: no label, no trade, no signal, and no opt-in.
- Data integrity hardening done on 2026-05-17: generic `ingest_block()` no longer double-counts wallet aggregates when the same block is re-ingested. Replays can still read the block, but wallet `total_tx`, `total_swaps`, and `total_volume` only move for newly inserted raw rows.
- Simple meaning: our local data is safer to collect in repeated bounded batches. This helps future trace/data work because re-runs should not create fake wallet activity.
- Amount USD safety gate active: after stablecoin-side repair of 3 poisoned rows, local swaps remain `277`, but only `237` swaps are scoreable for research scans/backtests. `40` rows are quarantined for decisions (`25` suspicious-large amount USD and `15` zero/missing amount USD). The rows stay visible for audit but no longer influence adaptive scans, backtests, local radar scoring, labels, mappings, trades, signals, or opt-ins.
- DEX trade curation checkpoint active: `/api/onchain/rpc/dex-trades-curated-schema-plan?dry_run=true` is read-only and measures whether local swaps can become a future clean `dex_trades_curated` fact table. Current smoke: `277` swaps, `237` scoreable amount USD rows, `240` exact-identity rows, `277` pool/router-present rows, `78` confident routes, and a small ready sample blocked only by missing raw log/event index. No table or row is created.
- Raw log provenance drilldown active: `/api/onchain/rpc/dex-trades-raw-log-provenance-drilldown?dry_run=true` is read-only and checks whether candidate curated swaps already have local transfer-log context. Current smoke over the top `20` rows: all `20` have local transfer context, token-pair transfer context, and pool-transfer context, but all still need bounded receipt replay to capture the actual Swap event `log_index`. Counts stayed unchanged; no RPC call and no write happened.
- Raw Swap proof curation has advanced: `dex_trade_raw_swap_provenance` contains `24` exact raw proof rows; `14` matched proofs now decode cleanly into token direction and human-readable amounts after targeted token metadata repair, while `10` ambiguous proofs remain blocked. `dex_trades_curated` now contains `14` decoded fact rows copied from those clean proofs. This is still data foundation only: no label, no mapping, no trade, no client signal, and no opt-in.
- Curated trade quality review is active: `/api/onchain/rpc/dex-trades-curated/review?dry_run=true` returns the `14` curated rows as `usable_for_research`, with `14` ready for shadow-scoring preview, `0` blocked, `14` venue-bound rows, and `13` infrastructure-side symbol gaps safely inferred as WBNB/USDC/USDT-style infrastructure sides. This means the batch is good enough for research/shadow scoring design, not client signals or trades.
- Curated DEX shadow scoring plan is active: `/api/onchain/rpc/dex-trades-curated/shadow-scoring-plan?dry_run=true` turns the 14 clean rows into `12` candidate token groups. Top groups include `STAR` with 3 curated rows and `ODY` with 2, but every group remains `research_only_needs_more_history` for policy/client use because the batch is too small, wallet diversity is too thin, outcomes are not backtested on curated facts, and slippage/liquidity execution risk is not modeled. Client signals/trades remain off.
- Source-backed curated expansion is active and now has one extra clean row: source-backed history collection added bounded raw context around clean curated facts, then raw Swap replay added one provenance row for HAQI, and curated insert promoted exactly one new decoded fact. `dex_trade_raw_swap_provenance=29` and `dex_trades_curated=19`. This is data foundation only: no label, no mapping, no trade, no client signal, and no opt-in.
- Unknown-router bounded history collection has now run two bounded passes around recent Unknown DEX router context. The latest pass added raw context only: +1 block, +44 transactions, +1 swap, and +135 token transfers. The result improved local context but still did not create a source-backed router mapping.
- Token metadata enrichment resolved 61 additional observed token contracts across the latest passes and wrote only `token_metadata` plus `data_jobs` audit rows. More metadata repair is still needed because 95 observed token symbols remain unresolved, but the main next bottleneck is now Unknown DEX/router proof.
- Latest exact swap/transfer micro-batch selected ETH and added raw context only: +1 block, +40 transactions, +27 token transfers, and +71 wallets. It did not add swaps, labels, mappings, trades, signals, or opt-ins.
- Latest Unknown DEX route/proof audit was read-only and found the important blocker: the top 10 unknown router-like addresses are not mapping-safe. Role classification returned `0` official routers, `6` intermediary-contract-like rows, `4` still unknown rows, `0` rows allowed for future mapping, and `0` client-ready signals. This means the next useful work is route/provenance repair and official-source proof, not more review queues and not trades.
- Unknown DEX route provenance workbench is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-route-provenance-workbench`. Latest BSC smoke with `limit=10` returned `ready_read_only`, reviewed 10 routers, covered 139 local swap rows, found 6 context-only/intermediary routes, 4 identity-first routes, 0 official routers, 0 mapping-ready rows, and 0 client-ready signals. It creates no evidence, mapping, label, trade, signal, or opt-in.
- Unknown DEX route provenance dossier is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-route-provenance-dossier`. Latest BSC dossier for top router `0x07964f135f276412b3182a3b2407b8dd45000000` returned `ready_read_only`, classifies the route as `intermediary_contract`, and covers 28 local swap rows, 27 transactions, 27 pools, and 3 wallets. Decision: context/path repair only; `safe_for_mapping_now=false`, `safe_for_scoring_now=false`, `safe_for_client_signal_now=false`, and `writes_performed=0`.
- Unknown DEX intermediary path repair plan is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-intermediary-path-repair-plan`. Latest BSC smoke for `0x07964f135f276412b3182a3b2407b8dd45000000` returned `ready_read_only`, sampled 8 transactions, read 58 local token-transfer rows, found 8 candidate underlying pools and 31 external counterparties, with 8 pair-bound sample rows. Simple meaning: this gives concrete path-repair leads, but still not an official DEX mapping, not a manipulation verdict, not a client signal, and not a trade. Required next proof remains bounded trace/internal-counterparty collection plus official underlying pool/router source proof.
- Unknown DEX intermediary bounded trace collection is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-intermediary-bounded-trace-collection`. Latest BSC dry-run for `0x07964f135f276412b3182a3b2407b8dd45000000` planned 2 exact trace calls with zero writes. Confirmed read-only trace attempted 2 calls and both failed with `missing trie node`, meaning the current RPC cannot trace those older transactions from available state. Simple meaning: route repair is now blocked by trace provider capability, not by code plumbing. Next safe lane is targeted explorer/internal-transaction fallback or an archive/debug-capable RPC, still read-only and still no mapping/scoring/trade.
- Unknown DEX intermediary internal-transaction fallback is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-intermediary-internal-transaction-fallback`. Latest BSC confirmed read-only fallback for `0x07964f135f276412b3182a3b2407b8dd45000000` attempted 2 Blockscout internal-transaction calls and both returned HTTP `404`. No internal counterparties were recovered, no writes occurred, and mapping/scoring/client signal stayed blocked. Simple meaning: for this older 0x07964 route, free public trace/fallback sources are not enough; the next useful options are archive/debug RPC, another explorer/internal source, or focusing on fresher Unknown DEX routes that are traceable.
- Unknown DEX traceability selector is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-traceability-candidate-selector`. Latest BSC smoke with `block_window=10000&limit=8` returned `ready_read_only`, scanned 11 recent Unknown DEX candidates, returned 8, and found 8 probe-ready routes with local transaction, transfer and pair-token context. Top fresh route: router `0x6b5e6445b2430e3d9bba509147589e83ec0b13db`, tx `0xa9864308d90258e5abff1b5087ab7c789c4bd31967f62ffe0c03371a903a551e`, symbols `UPEPE`/`PEPE`, 16 local transfer rows, pair tokens bound, score 96. This is a route-repair target only, not a signal or trade.
- Unknown DEX traceability candidate internal probe is now active at `/api/onchain/rpc/unknown-dex-traceability-candidate-internal-probe`. Latest BSC confirmed read-only probe attempted the top 3 selector-ranked routes and all 3 Blockscout calls returned HTTP `404`; no internals were recovered and no writes occurred. Simple meaning: the selector now finds better candidates, but Blockscout BSC still does not provide internal transactions for the sampled txs. Next useful work is either archive/debug RPC, alternative explorer/source route, or collecting fresher blocks where internals are available.

