## Latest Product Direction - Agent OS Lite

- Added `rag/memory/core_equity_agent_os_lite.md`.
- Simple decision: yes, Core Equity should move toward an agentic OS, but as **Agent OS Lite**, not as an unrestricted AI operating system.
- The current safe design is Codex-operated, policy-gated, task-contract based, audit-first, and focused on data improvement.
- Agent OS Lite means: one allowed task, one validation, one audit receipt, then stop.
- It is not a trading bot, not a Hermes/CrewAI takeover, not a self-modifying system, not a label writer, and not a mapping writer.
- Current foundation already exists: control plane, task contracts, one-task runner dry-run, audit preview, confirmed audit-only write, schedule plan, and paused automation card.
- Next useful Agent OS Lite components:
  - agent state snapshot;
  - read-only task queue view;
  - cycle policy gate;
  - audit receipt ledger;
  - paused schedule control.
- Product focus remains data quality first: source-backed candidates, route/source proof, token metadata repair, bounded exact raw data, repeatability, and backtest readiness.
- Safety result: no runtime code changed for this direction note, no DB write, no schedule enabled, no label, no DEX evidence, no mapping, no trade, no client signal, and no opt-in.
- Next safest step: build an Agent OS Lite state snapshot endpoint/read-only report, or keep improving the current data tasks manually before enabling any recurring cycle.

